course: dictionary
lesson: 8802
title: Shave: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shave can mean more than one thing, so context tells you which meaning you need. Look at the words around it. In «Kieran gets his own haircut, with a shaved line», the word line tells you hair is cut very close to the skin.
explain: The most common meaning is to cut hair very close to the skin with a razor. Many men shave their face each day. Some people shave their legs or their heads too.
explain: Shave can also mean to cut very thin pieces off something, like «shave chocolate». A close shave is a noun phrase meaning you only just avoid danger. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "nearly had an accident" should still make sense.
fact: Shave means to cut hair very close to the skin with a razor.
fact: Shave also means to cut very thin pieces off something, such as chocolate.
fact: A close shave means you only just avoid danger.
fact: Shaving does not make hair grow back thicker, darker or faster. That is a myth, because stubble only feels rough.
fact: Hair is dead keratin, the same material as nails. Only the root under the skin is alive.
exercise: «Kieran gets his own haircut, with a shaved line.» What does shaved mean here? | Washed and dried | Painted in bright colours | *Cut very close to the skin | Plaited into a long braid
exercise: Mum says, «I nearly had a close shave on the stairs.» What does she mean? | She had a haircut at the barber's | *She only just avoided an accident | She fell down and hurt her knee | She cut a thin slice of cake
exercise: «Shave some chocolate over the pudding» uses shave in a different way. Which sentence uses shave the same way? | Dad will shave his beard tonight | Dad shaves his face every morning | *Dad will shave some cheese over the pasta | Dad had a close shave on his bike
test: Why does shaving not make hair grow back thicker? | Hair grows faster after every close shave | Shaving cuts the root, so the hair grows back thicker | *Hair is dead keratin, and only the root under the skin is alive | Stubble feels rough, so it must be thicker
test: In «a shaved forehead», what does shaved mean? | Covered by a hat | *Cut very close to the skin | Painted gold | Wrapped in a long braid
exam: Which phrase means you only just avoid danger? | a clean shave | shave chocolate | *a close shave | shave off
